00:33:04,615 --> 00:33:10,615
Hellraiser: Bloodline (also known as Hellraiser IV: Bloodline) is a 1996 American science fiction horror film
and the fourth installment in the Hellraiser series, which serves as both a prequel and a sequel.

11
00:36:23,076 --> 00:36:29,076
Directed by Kevin Yagher and Joe Chappelle, the film stars Doug Bradley as Pinhead,
reprising his role and now the only remaining original character and cast member.

12
00:39:41,538 --> 00:39:47,538
It also features Bruce Ramsay, Valentina Vargas, Kim Myers
and Adam Scott in his first major film role.

13
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
It was the last Hellraiser film to be released theatrically and the last to have any major
official involvement with series creator Clive Barker until the 2022 reboot.

14
00:46:18,461 --> 00:46:24,461
In the 18th century, Phillip LeMarchand a celebrated toymaker (Ramsay) is hired to create his greatest work, the Lament Configuration,
not knowing that it will allow the summoning of the demonic Cenobites, including Pinhead (Bradley) and Angelique (Vargas).

15
00:49:36,923 --> 00:49:42,923
Hundreds of years in the future, the toymaker's descendant Dr.

16
00:52:55,384 --> 00:53:01,384
Paul Merchant (also played by Ramsay), an engineer, has designed a space
station that he believes can trap and destroy the Cenobites.

17
00:56:13,846 --> 00:56:19,846
Major themes include time, toys and game-playing, adultery and slavery.

18
00:59:32,307 --> 00:59:38,307
The film had a troubled history and, after completing the film, original director Yagher
left the production when distributor Miramax demanded new scenes be shot.

19
01:02:50,769 --> 01:02:56,769
It was subsequently completed by Chappelle.

20
01:06:09,230 --> 01:06:15,230
The new scenes and re-shoots changed several characters' relationships, gave the
film a happy ending, introduced Pinhead earlier, and cut 25 minutes.

21
01:09:27,692 --> 01:09:33,692
Yagher felt the changes diverged too strongly from his vision and was granted the Alan
Smithee pseudonym, an alias used by directors who want to go uncredited.

22
01:12:46,153 --> 01:12:52,153
Miramax released it in the United States on March
8, where it grossed $9 million.

23
01:16:04,615 --> 01:16:10,615
It was not screened for critics and received negative reviews.

24
01:19:23,076 --> 01:19:29,076
The film explores themes of artificial intelligence
(a.i.), hell, engineer, pinhead, demon.

25
01:22:41,538 --> 01:22:47,538
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
